 "title": "Collagen, C–H 1728 nm band (narrow contrast)",
 "short_name": "C–H 1728 nm",
 "kind": "regression",
 "role": "collagen_percent",
 "description": "Reads collagen from the C–H band at 1728 nm as a narrow contrast: the second derivative (SG35 cubic) of log10(1/R) averaged over 1726-1730 nm minus the mean of the two shoulders at 1716-1720 and 1736-1740 nm, turned into % collagen by a straight line fitted on the 140 reference bones. On clean bone it agrees with the N–H models; extra organic material with C–H but no nitrogen (lipid, wax, many consolidants) raises it above them. The app compares it with CONS3 for the C–H note and never uses it for the verdict.",
 "citation": {
  "text": "SPYDER Bone (C–H 1728 nm); calibration data Ryder, C. et al. 2026. Refining near-infrared spectroscopy for collagen quantification in archaeological bone. Journal of Archaeological Science 185:106448 (calibration spectra and yields: supplement mmc2).",
  "doi": "10.1016/j.jas.2025.106448"
 },
 "authors": [
  "M. Sponheimer (PI)"
 ],
 "created": "2026-10-18",
